// ============================================================================
// chi2-critical-values.epher -- chi-square cut points for levels and df
//
// The chi-square cut points x such that P(chi2 <= x) equals the
// probability in `p` with the given degrees of freedom, from the builtin
// invchi2 (guide 1.20). The 95th percentile with 5 df is the 11.0705 of
// goodness-of-fit tests. The last lines feed each cut point back through
// chi2cdf: the lower-tail area at the cut point comes back to p.
//
// Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/statistics/distributions/chi2-critical-values.epher"
// In the REPL:             load epher scripts/statistics/distributions/chi2-critical-values.epher
// Web/desktop:             paste the whole file into the entry, press Enter
// Everything also works line by line in the TUI.
//
// No knobs: the levels and degrees of freedom below are the demonstration.
// ============================================================================

// ---- the cut points -------------------------------------------------------------------
print("invchi2(0.95, 5):", invchi2(0.95, 5))      // the 5% chi2 with 5 df
print("invchi2(0.975, 10):", invchi2(0.975, 10))  // the 2.5% chi2 with 10 df
print("invchi2(0.99, 20):", invchi2(0.99, 20))    // the 1% chi2 with 20 df

// ---- each cut point fed back through the cdf comes back to its probability ------------
print("chi2cdf(invchi2(0.95, 5), 5):", chi2cdf(invchi2(0.95, 5), 5))
print("chi2cdf(invchi2(0.99, 20), 20):", chi2cdf(invchi2(0.99, 20), 20))

// ---- expected output ----
// = invchi2(0.95, 5): 11.0704976935
// = invchi2(0.975, 10): 20.4831773509
// = invchi2(0.99, 20): 37.5662347867
// = chi2cdf(invchi2(0.95, 5), 5): 0.95
// = chi2cdf(invchi2(0.99, 20), 20): 0.99